WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:04.560
Speaker 1: I want to talk about a&nbsp;
bit of news from a few days ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:10.080
which is quite interesting. There is now a report&nbsp;
that President Joe Biden told former President&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:17.960
Barack Obama that he is going to run in 2024, that&nbsp;
Joe Biden will run for reelection in 2024. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:24.880
is a report in The Guardian from a few days ago&nbsp;
which has a subheadline. The president, Joe Biden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:30.720
thinks he's the only one who can beat Trump,&nbsp;
according to what a source told The Hill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.840
as Trump readies his own third run, the&nbsp;
article reads, Joe Biden has told Barack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.880
Obama he will run for reelection in 2024,&nbsp;
according to the Washington website The Hill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.080
the site cited two anonymous sources. One&nbsp;
was quoted as saying Biden wants to run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:51.440
and he's clearly letting everyone know. It&nbsp;
wasn't clear when Biden told Obama his plan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.360
but Obama did visit the White House earlier&nbsp;
this month to celebrate the Affordable Care Act.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.160
We know that Joe Biden used to be the&nbsp;
vice president at 78. Biden was the oldest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.080
president ever inaugurated. If he won again,&nbsp;
he would be 82 at the start of his second term.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:12.240
In September. It was widely reported Biden&nbsp;
and aides told allies he planned to run again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:17.600
in December. Biden said he would run if he stayed&nbsp;
in good health. He also said Kamala Harris as VP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:23.200
would be on the ticket again. In a December&nbsp;
interview with ABC. Biden said another Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:30.720
candidacy would increase the prospect of running&nbsp;
in Brussels in March. Biden referred to Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.840
when he said In the next election, I'd be&nbsp;
very fortunate if I had the same man running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:42.080
against me. Do I think Joe Biden is going to run&nbsp;
again? I actually don't know. I at this point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:50.080
I believe that Joe Biden has to say it is&nbsp;
my intention to run for reelection. I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:56.240
have any doubt that that is the correct thing to&nbsp;
say. It would be problematic for his presidency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:02.080
now to say I'm not even going to run again. It&nbsp;
would be a news cycle, a serious news cycle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.640
It would interfere with whatever it is Joe&nbsp;
Biden plans to try to do in what's left of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.920
his first term. So I think that no matter what his&nbsp;
intentions are, this is what he would be saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:20.160
right now, whether he will ultimately run. I don't&nbsp;
know. Now, the question of who could beat Trump.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.760
We actually do have some polling. And I know that&nbsp;
looking at polling this early is a bit fraught.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:32.240
But we have a number of different polls which can&nbsp;
give us some information. Many of these are from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:39.680
the last few days in a hypothetical Biden versus&nbsp;
Trump matchup. The Morning Consult Politico poll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:46.320
has Biden 45 and Trump 44. Now, you could argue&nbsp;
that's not great because Trump isn't even really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.960
a candidate. You could also say Trump really kind&nbsp;
of is a candidate because everybody thinks he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:59.840
running in an insider advantage. Poll a Trump is&nbsp;
defeating Biden. 4743. There is a YouGov Yahoo!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:08.880
News poll where it's Biden 43, Trump 41. And then&nbsp;
there's also other polls like Bernie versus Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:16.000
where Trump bests Bernie by one in morning&nbsp;
consult. So I don't know that these polls at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.440
this point, given that we don't know if Biden's&nbsp;
running and we don't know if Trump is running,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.960
I don't know how much they tell us other than it's&nbsp;
not obvious anybody's going to run away with it. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:32.800
think that's the fair takeaway from what we have&nbsp;
from polling so far. If it's Biden versus Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:38.800
there is a fight and either candidate could win.&nbsp;
If it's not Trump and it's Kamala Harris, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.800
conceivable that either one could win. If&nbsp;
it's not Trump or Biden, and instead it's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:51.600
for example, Harris DeSantis, as the Harris poll&nbsp;
asked. Right now it's Harris plus four. So I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.560
it's too early for any of these polls to tell us&nbsp;
anything definitive other than there's uncertainty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:02.960
about who the candidates will be. And there's&nbsp;
a real question mark as to who voters would,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:09.280
in theory, rally behind. I think that we just&nbsp;
don't know. What I want to hear from you is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

